Unlike `_takeConfigEntry` (coverage-driven), this one is **fully covered** — CRAP = CC = 13, so no test can fix it; the cyclomatic complexity itself must come down (threshold 12.0, ratchet is down-only). Extract the per-rune allowlist into a predicate:

```dart
void validateModelIdShape(String modelId) {
  final id = modelId.trim();
  String fail(String why) =>
      throw ConfigException('invalid model id "$modelId": $why');
  if (id.isEmpty) fail('the model id is empty');
  if (id.length > 200) fail('longer than 200 characters');
  if (id.contains('://')) fail('URL schemes are not model ids');
  for (final rune in id.runes) {
    if (!_isModelIdRune(rune)) {
      fail('"${String.fromCharCode(rune)}" is not a model id character');
    }
  }
}

/// ASCII label chars, the label punctuation set, and any non-ASCII letter.
bool _isModelIdRune(int rune) =>
    (rune >= 0x30 && rune <= 0x39) || // 0-9
    (rune >= 0x41 && rune <= 0x5a) || // A-Z
    (rune >= 0x61 && rune <= 0x7a) || // a-z
    rune >= 0x80 || // non-ASCII letters/digits pass
    const {'.', '_', '-', '/', ':', '@', '+', '~'}
        .contains(String.fromCharCode(rune));
```

While there: `rune >= 0x80` admits the **C1 control range U+0080–U+009F** (NEL, CSI…), so the doc comment's "no whitespace or control characters" claim is not fully enforced. Consider rejecting `rune >= 0x80 && rune <= 0x9f` (and `String.trim()` already strips most — but not all — Unicode whitespace before this loop).

